{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"J5 c97f -> PLAN REVIEW PASS (0 blocking, 1 advisory), attestation certified. J5 is independent of J2 so it was reviewable now.\nEPIC REVIEW #7 -> BLOCK 1 (E1/COH): correct — remediation #5 added reconciler.resolved_statuses to the plan BODY but I never wrote an AC for it, so an implementer could omit it and still pass. Added the AC (validated list-of-strings key, {Resolved,Done,Cancelled} default, probe classifies against it).\nApplied epic advisories:\n - ADV4 (G6) was the sharpest: outbound_fields.py is loaded via spec_from_file_location under SYNTHETIC names with NO package context, so a new import for the single-sourced maps could break that load mode. INVESTIGATED EMPIRICALLY rather than assuming: loaded jira_fields.py (which already uses absolute 'from rebar_reconciler.adapters.jira.adf import ...') under a synthetic '_parity_probe' name -> imports resolve fine, __package__ == '' , because the package conftest puts the engine dir on sys.path. So ABSOLUTE imports are safe; a RELATIVE one ('from ..jira_family import') would raise 'attempted relative import with no known parent package'. Recorded that as a hard constraint in J2 plus a test that loads each edited pinned module by path to prove it.\n   Correction to an earlier note of mine: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_config.py:192 DOES load adapters/jira/jira_fields.py by path (as _parity_<file>). That does not change the move plan — the synthetic-name load resolves absolute imports and does not pin the file's location the way _loader.lazy_load does — but the file is not entirely free of by-path references as I earlier stated.\n - ADV2 (T3): the epic body described the oracle vaguely as 'Dockerized Jira from the Atlassian SDK'; J5 pins pycontribs/jira-test-image:8.17.1. Named the exact image/run command/URL in the epic and cross-referenced J5, incl. why 8.17.1 (>= 8.14 = PAT support) and its stated version-drift limitation.\n - ADV5 (T5c): declared PAT secret handling at the parent level — JIRA_PAT is env-only, never accepted from committed [tool.rebar.jira] config, never logged, and a missing value fails loud instead of degrading to anonymous. Consistent with J6, which already specified env-only.\n - ADV3 (T7) was already applied to J8 last pass; ADV1 (P6) generic, skipped."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785295827508984001,"uuid":"c29c5209-bf86-4e39-8a1a-38bb818248d9"}